{"kind":"request","text":"ARC-1: an admitted entry must be archivable. Build after the\ncutover head (05d618e2) lands.\n\nThe fact, from builder act ee05b30b. `ARCHIVE_BOUNDS.attempts` is\n512 for one pass, and `inputWork` is 64 MiB. An entry of 128 uses\nneeds 4 attempts for each use and 3 for each foreign sequence, so\nit needs more than 512. Its copies also need more than\n`inputWork`. Validation admits that entry, and the archive cannot\ncopy it in one pass.\n\nWork:\n1. Measure. Run one fixture with the widest entry that the\n   bounds admit, and record what the archive does: the reason,\n   the attempts, the work units, and whether the floor stops.\n2. Propose one rule in a short note and stop for my ruling\n   before you build it. The candidates: the archive copies the\n   uses of one entry across passes, or validation bounds the uses\n   of one entry by what one pass can copy, or the archive caps\n   follow from `usesPerEntry` and `entryBytes`.\n3. Build the ruled rule with a test at the widest admitted entry.","body":{"conditions":"Build after the cutover head 05d618e2 lands. Step 2 stops for a planner ruling. No cap changes without that ruling. Gate once before review.","target_head":"64112e4576b4c3c8fb668389786deb6b703da417","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}